# Supabase Configuration
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-id.supabase.co
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-public-key-here

# === GOOGLE SIGN-IN (native Android) ==========================
#
# The *Web* OAuth client id from your Google Cloud project. This is
# the same client id you registered as the Authorized Client ID in
# Supabase Auth -> Providers -> Google. Used by the native Android
# Google Sign-In SDK as the serverClientId so the returned ID token
# is acceptable to Supabase's verifier.
#
# You also need an *Android* OAuth client id in the same Cloud
# project, with package name app.volyume and SHA-1 matching the
# signing certificate of the APK that ships to testers. For Play
# internal testing this is the Play App Signing certificate (Play
# Console -> Setup -> App signing -> App signing key certificate).
# No env var holds the Android client id, but Google requires it
# exists for the package + SHA-1 pair to be trusted.
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID=

# === SENTRY (error + performance monitoring) ===
#
# 1. Create a project at https://sentry.io/ — pick "React Native".
# 2. Copy the DSN from Settings → Projects → <name> → Client Keys.
# 3. Paste it below. EAS Build picks it up via this env var, no
#    secrets file needed.
#    eas secret:create --scope project --name EXPO_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN --value "https://...@sentry.io/..."
#
# Without this DSN, the Sentry SDK silently no-ops. Errors still
# land in the on-device ring buffer (Settings → Debug logs) but
# don't reach the cloud dashboard.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=

# === DOMAIN SETUP (volyume.app) ===
#
# 1. In Supabase dashboard → Authentication → URL Configuration
#    - Site URL:      https://volyume.app
#    - Redirect URLs: volyume://
#                     https://volyume.app/**
#
# 2. For custom email auth (optional):
#    Settings → Auth → SMTP Settings
#    - Use white-labeled SMTP from noreply@volyume.app
#    - Customize email templates to point to https://volyume.app
#
# 3. Universal linking (automatic once domain is set):
#    - iOS: .well-known/apple-app-site-association (see DOMAIN_SETUP.md)
#    - Android: .well-known/assetlinks.json (see DOMAIN_SETUP.md)
#
# See DOMAIN_SETUP.md for full setup instructions
